{"id": "210740", "revid": "2183461", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=210740", "title": "Wangerland", "text": "Wangerland is a municipality in East Frisia, in the northwest part of Lower Saxony in Germany.\nGet in.\nWangerland is accessible primarily by car, train, or bus, with the closest major transport hubs being in Wilhelmshaven or Jever. \nBy car.\nBy car, the most common route is via the A29 motorway towards Wilhelmshaven. \nBy plane.\nThe closest major airports are Bremen Airport (') and Hamburg Airport ('). From either airport, take a train to Wilhelmshaven, then continue by bus to Wangerland.\nBy train.\nThe nearest railway station is in or, served by regional trains from Oldenburg or Bremen. From Wilhelmshaven, you can transfer to local buses to reach Wangerland\u2019s coastal towns like Horumersiel or Hooksiel.\nBy bus.\nLong-distance services like FlixBus operate to Wilhelmshaven or Jever from cities like Hamburg or Bremen."}
